  "title": "Atisha’s journey to Tibet",
  "summary": "The Buddhist scholar Atisa, steward of the Vikramasila college, left for Tibet in 1040 after an invitation from Nag tsho. He spent a year in Nepal, arrived in Guge in 1042, then travelled to central Tibet and finally to Narthang, where he died. He worked mainly in western Tibet at first and later travelled widely, and he and his disciples corrected and revised Tibetan translations of Buddhist texts.",
